 @end defun
+
+On NS frames, explicitly specifying @code{:background nil} for a color
+image whose type supports that property makes the image respect the
+frame's @code{alpha-background} parameter.  This is useful for images
+which draw shaped extensions of a face background: transparent pixels
+show the underlying background, while opaque pixels retain the same
+background opacity.  Omitting @code{:background} leaves image opacity
+unchanged.
+
 @node XBM Images
 @subsection XBM Images
 @cindex XBM
@@ -6619,7 +6628,8 @@ SVG Images
 @item :background @var{background}
 @var{background}, if non-@code{nil}, should be a string specifying a
 color, which is used as the image's background color if the image
-supports transparency.  If the value is @code{nil}, it defaults to the
+supports transparency.  On NS displays, a @code{nil} value preserves
+the image's transparency.  On other displays, it defaults to the
 current face's background color.
 
 @item :css @var{css}
@@ -7093,6 +7103,10 @@ Other Image Types
 
 @item PNG
 Image type @code{png}.
+The @code{:background} property can specify a color against which
+transparent pixels are flattened.  On NS displays, a @code{nil} value
+preserves the image's transparency.  On other displays, it defaults to
+the frame's background color.
 
 @item TIFF
 Image type @code{tiff}.
@@ -7101,6 +7115,7 @@ Other Image Types
 @item WebP
 Image type @code{webp}.
 Supports the @code{:index} property.  @xref{Multi-Frame Images}.
+The @code{:background} property behaves as for PNG images.
 @end table
 
 @node Defining Images
