 * Changes in Emacs 32.1
 
++++
+** NS image loaders preserve source transparency.
+Native images and the specialized SVG and WebP loaders now retain
+their alpha channels when the ':background' image property is nil.
+A non-nil background color flattens transparent pixels against that
+color.
+
++++
+** NS images can respect 'alpha-background'.
+A color-image descriptor that explicitly specifies ':background nil'
+is now composited without increasing the alpha of the background
+beneath it.  Omitting the property retains the usual image opacity.
+
